From 52ea3523cd1cfc93fdf9b378b9b6fa75b70769da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:57:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(logging): websockets keepalive drops Hermes already
 handles log one INFO line, not ERROR + traceback [daveey]

websockets' keepalive thread/task logs a peer that stopped answering pings as
`ERROR websockets.client: keepalive ping failed` + traceback, even though the
connection is already failed and the caller handles it (Kanban sync's FeedWatcher
reconnects in 1 s and polling covers the gap). errors.log then reads like an
unhandled crash and self-heal files it as a defect (agent-ac35b4d534: hub
2026-10-27 20:49:20Z, MacBook 16:08 PT; the Board drops every feed socket
together several times a day).

- hermes_cli/ws_logging.py: ws_logger(side) wraps the library's own
  `websockets.<side>` logger (level/handler config unchanged) and turns that one
  message into an INFO line naming the cause; every other record keeps its level.
- Every websockets connect()/serve() in production code passes logger=ws_logger():
  kanban_sync_client FeedWatcher, tui_gateway event_publisher, transcription and
  TTS streaming, browser CDP tool + supervisor, relay ws_transport, buzz, simplex,
  google_meet (realtime, node client/server). yuanbao dials with
  ping_interval=None (no keepalive), so it stays as is (grandfathered).
- code_health HX015: a websockets connect()/serve() without logger= in production
  code is a new finding, so the next call site cannot reintroduce the ERROR
  (a pytest source scanner is banned by tests/AGENTS.md).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_feed_keepalive.py (real server behind a relay
that goes silent after the upgrade: FeedWatcher reconnects, zero ERROR records;
red on fd394a4611 with the production traceback), test_ws_logging.py,
tests/scripts/test_code_health_ws_rule.py.
---
